A ramp has a sloping length of $15$ m and rises $9$ m. Find its angle $\theta$ with the horizontal, correct to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,3);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.7,0)--(3.7,0.3)--(4,0.3);
\path (4,1.5) node[right] {$9\text{ m}$};
\path (2,1.5) node[above left] {$15\text{ m}$};
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=36.87,radius=0.7];
\path (0.95,0.28) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find $\theta$, correct to the nearest minute.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4,0);\coordinate (C) at (4,3);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.7,0)--(3.7,0.3)--(4,0.3);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (2,1.5) node[above left] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=36.87,radius=0.7];
\path (0.95,0.28) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

All three sides are given. Find $\theta$, correct to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (3.6,0);\coordinate (C) at (3.6,1.5);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (3.3,0)--(3.3,0.3)--(3.6,0.3);
\path (1.8,0) node[below] {$24\text{ cm}$};
\path (3.6,0.75) node[right] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.8,0.75) node[above left] {$26\text{ cm}$};
\draw (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=22.62,radius=0.8];
\path (1.1,0.23) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A road rises at a grade of $2$ in $9$: it rises $2$ m for every $9$ m measured horizontally. Find its angle $\theta$ with the horizontal, correct to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (C) at (4.5,1);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (4.25,0)--(4.25,0.25)--(4.5,0.25);
\path (2.25,0) node[below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\path (4.5,0.5) node[right] {$2\text{ m}$};
\draw (1.1,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=12.53,radius=1.1];
\path (1.5,0.19) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A straight roof joins two vertical walls of heights $4.6$ m and $2.8$ m. The walls are $4.5$ m apart horizontally. Find the angle $\theta$ that the roof makes with the horizontal, correct to the nearest minute.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (C) at (0,4.6);\coordinate (D) at (4.5,2.8);\coordinate (E) at (0,2.8);
\draw (A)--(C)--(D)--(B)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (E)--(D);
\draw (0,3.05)--(0.25,3.05)--(0.25,2.8);
\path (0,2.3) node[left] {$4.6\text{ m}$};
\path (4.5,1.4) node[right] {$2.8\text{ m}$};
\path (2.25,0) node[below] {$4.5\text{ m}$};
\draw (3.7,2.8) arc[start angle=180,end angle=158.2,radius=0.8];
\path (3.35,3.03) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
